  <h2 id="agreement">1. The agreement</h2>
  <p>
    These terms form an agreement between Big Tree Services ("we", "us", "our") and the company that
    subscribes to our CRM ("you", "your"). They apply every time you or your staff access the
    application. By creating an account, signing in or using the application, you accept them. If you
    are accepting on behalf of a company, you confirm you have authority to bind it.
  </p>
  <p>
    The application is provided for business use only and is not offered to consumers. Users must be
    at least 18 years old.
  </p>

  <h2 id="service">2. The service</h2>
  <p>
    We provide a hosted web application for managing tree care work: estimates and site visits, tree
    inventories and photographs, quoting, scheduling and crew dispatch, invoicing, receipts, hours
    and equipment tracking, and reporting. We provide it on a subscription basis for the term agreed
    with you.
  </p>
  <p>
    We may add, change or remove features. If we remove or materially degrade a feature you rely on,
    we will give you reasonable notice.
  </p>

  <h2 id="accounts">3. Accounts and access</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You are responsible for every account issued under your organisation, for the accuracy of the
      information in it, and for everything done through it.
    </li>
    <li>
      Accounts are personal to the individual. Credentials must not be shared, and you must tell us
      promptly at <a href="mailto:info@bigtreeservices.ca">info@bigtreeservices.ca</a> if you believe
      an account has been compromised.
    </li>
    <li>
      Your administrators control who has an account and what permissions they hold. You must remove
      access promptly when someone leaves your organisation.
    </li>
    <li>
      We may suspend an account immediately where we reasonably believe it presents a security risk
      or is being used in breach of these terms.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="acceptable">4. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You and your users must not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>use the application unlawfully, or to store or send unlawful, infringing or harmful content;</li>
    <li>upload malware, or attempt to breach, probe or circumvent the security of the application;</li>
    <li>attempt to access another organisation's data;</li>
    <li>reverse engineer, decompile or copy the application, or resell or sublicense access to it;</li>
    <li>use automated means to scrape it or to place unreasonable load on it;</li>
    <li>use it to send unsolicited bulk email; or</li>
    <li>enter payment card numbers, government identification numbers or health information into
        free-text fields.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="yourdata">5. Your data</h2>
  <p>
    The records you enter &mdash; customers, sites, tree inventories, photographs, quotes, invoices,
    hours and everything else &mdash; remain <strong>your data</strong>. We claim no ownership of it.
  </p>
  <p>
    You grant us the limited licence needed to host, process, transmit, back up and display that data
    in order to operate the application for you, and to do so through the service providers named in
    the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    You are responsible for the accuracy and lawfulness of the data you enter, including having a
    lawful basis to hold the personal information of your own customers and staff and to send them
    the messages you send through the application. We handle that data as your processor, in
    accordance with the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can export your data from the application at any time while your account is active. We keep
    backups as part of normal operation, but <strong>you remain responsible for retaining your own
    copies of records you need to keep</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="email">6. Email sending</h2>
  <p>
    If you connect a Google Workspace or Microsoft 365 mailbox, you authorise us to send messages
    from that address on your behalf &mdash; quotes, invoices, receipts, appointment notices and job
    updates generated by the application.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You confirm you are entitled to authorise sending from that mailbox and, where it is not your
      own, that you have the mailbox owner's permission.
    </li>
    <li>
      You are responsible for the content of messages sent from your account and for complying with
      anti-spam law, including Canada's Anti-Spam Legislation (CASL) and, where relevant, CAN-SPAM
      and the GDPR. That includes having the consent you need to email each recipient and honouring
      unsubscribe requests.
    </li>
    <li>
      Delivery depends on your mail provider and on the recipient's mail systems. We cannot
      guarantee that a message will be delivered, will not be filtered as spam, or will be delivered
      at a particular time.
    </li>
    <li>
      We may suspend sending from your account if it appears to be generating spam complaints or
      breaching your mail provider's terms.
    </li>
    <li>
      You may disconnect the mailbox at any time. Doing so stops the application from sending mail.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="thirdparty">7. Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    The application relies on third-party services to function, including Nylas for email delivery,
    Amazon Web Services for hosting and file storage, and Google and Microsoft where you connect a
    mailbox. Your use of a connected mailbox is also subject to that provider's own terms. We are not
    responsible for the acts, omissions or availability of third-party services, but we will use
    reasonable care in selecting them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="fees">8. Fees</h2>
  <p>
    Fees, the billing period and the number of users covered are as set out in the order or
    subscription agreed with you. Fees are payable in advance and are non-refundable except where the
    law requires otherwise or we have agreed otherwise in writing. Fees are exclusive of taxes, which
    you are responsible for. We may change our fees on 30 days' notice, effective from your next
    renewal. We may suspend access to accounts more than 30 days in arrears after giving you notice.
  </p>

  <h2 id="availability">9. Availability and support</h2>
  <p>
    We aim to keep the application available during business hours and to provide support by email at
    <a href="mailto:info@bigtreeservices.ca">info@bigtreeservices.ca</a>, responding within five
    business days. Unless we have signed a separate service level agreement with you, the application
    is provided without a guaranteed uptime commitment. We may take it offline for maintenance, and
    will give advance notice of planned maintenance where practicable.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ip">10. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The application, its software, design, documentation and our trade marks are and remain our
    property. These terms grant you a non-exclusive, non-transferable right to use the application
    during your subscription, and nothing more. If you send us feedback or suggestions, we may use
    them freely and without obligation to you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="confidentiality">11. Confidentiality</h2>
  <p>
    Each party may receive information from the other that is confidential. Each will use the other's
    confidential information only to perform this agreement, will protect it with at least reasonable
    care, and will not disclose it except to staff and contractors who need it and are under similar
    obligations, or where the law requires disclosure. This does not apply to information that is
    public, already known, or independently developed without reference to the other party's
    information.
  </p>

  <h2 id="warranties">12. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
  <p>
    The application is provided <strong>"as is" and "as available"</strong>. To the fullest extent
    the law permits, we disclaim all warranties, express or implied, including merchantability,
    fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. We do not warrant that the application
    will be uninterrupted or error free, that defects will be corrected, or that it will meet your
    requirements.
  </p>
  <p>
    The application supports your business records and calculations, but it is not a substitute for
    professional judgement. It does not provide arboricultural, safety, legal, accounting or tax
    advice, and you remain responsible for the assessments, quotes, invoices and safety decisions you
    make using it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">13. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent the law permits, neither party is liable for indirect, incidental, special,
    consequential or punitive damages, or for lost profits, lost revenue, lost business or lost or
    corrupted data, however caused.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our total aggregate liability arising out of or relating to this agreement is limited to the fees
    you paid us in the twelve months before the event giving rise to the claim.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law, including for fraud or for
    death or personal injury caused by negligence.
  </p>

  <h2 id="indemnity">14. Indemnity</h2>
  <p>
    You will indemnify us against claims, losses and reasonable costs arising from your data, your
    use of the application in breach of these terms or the law, or messages sent from your account.
  </p>

  <h2 id="term">15. Term and termination</h2>
  <p>
    This agreement runs for your subscription term and renews as agreed until terminated. Either
    party may terminate on 30 days' written notice effective at the end of the current term, or
    immediately if the other party materially breaches these terms and does not fix the breach within
    30 days of notice. We may suspend or terminate immediately for non-payment beyond the period in
    section 8, or where required by law.
  </p>
  <p>
    On termination your right to use the application ends. We will keep your data available for
    export for <strong>90 days</strong>, after which we will delete or anonymise it as described in
    the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. Sections 5, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14 and 17 survive
    termination.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">16. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. The effective date at the top shows when they last changed. For
    material changes we will give at least 30 days' notice in the application or by email. Continuing
    to use the application after a change takes effect means you accept the updated terms; if you do
    not accept them, you may terminate before they take effect.
  </p>

